      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "aeefc483-d679-5529-ae3d-2d38d3d0801c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Buddy Baker, Bruce M. Fischer, Bill Bixby, Jack Clayton, Ray Bradbury, Paul J. Smith, Clint Eastwood\n- Companies: Walt Disney Productions\n- Films: The Apple Dumpling Gang, Something Wicked This Way Comes, The Outlaw Josey Wales, The Apple Dumpling Gang Rides Again, The Shaggy D.A., The Many Adventures of Winnie the Pooh, The Fox and the Hound\n- Topics: California Gold Rush, film music, adaptation\n\nFacts:\n- In 1975, Walt Disney Productions produced The Apple Dumpling Gang, an American comedy-western film about gambler Russell Donovan, played by Bill Bixby, who is tricked into caring for orphans who strike gold during the California Gold Rush.\n- In 1975, composer Buddy Baker, together with Paul J. Smith, scored the Disney film The Apple Dumpling Gang.\n- In 1976, Bruce M. Fischer played a rapist in Clint Eastwood's film The Outlaw Josey Wales.\n- In 1976, Buddy Baker, together with Paul J. Smith, scored the Disney film The Shaggy D.A.\n- In 1977, Buddy Baker, together with Paul J. Smith, scored the Disney film The Many Adventures of Winnie the Pooh.\n- In 1979, Buddy Baker, together with Paul J. Smith, scored the Disney film The Apple Dumpling Gang Rides Again.\n- In 1981, Buddy Baker, together with Paul J. Smith, scored the Disney film The Fox and the Hound.\n- In 1983, Walt Disney Productions produced Something Wicked This Way Comes, an American horror fantasy film directed by Jack Clayton from a screenplay by Ray Bradbury based on Bradbury's novel of the same name.\n- In 1983, Bruce M. Fischer played Mr. Coogar in Something Wicked This Way Comes.\n- Buddy Baker was an American composer who lived from January 4, 1918 to July 26, 2002.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "eaca8ffc-97c0-5647-8eb1-99e3df2173a6",
        "text": "Page: The Apple Dumpling Gang (film). Sentence: The Apple Dumpling Gang is a 1975 American comedy-western film produced by Walt Disney Productions about a slick gambler named Russell Donovan (Bill Bixby) who is duped into taking care of a group of orphans who eventually strike gold during the California Gold Rush.\nPage: Something Wicked This Way Comes (film). Sentence: Something Wicked This Way Comes is a 1983 American horror fantasy film directed by Jack Clayton and produced by Walt Disney Productions from a screenplay written by Ray Bradbury, based on his novel of the same name.\nPage: Buddy Baker (composer). Sentence: Norman Dale \"Buddy\" Baker (January 4, 1918 – July 26, 2002) was an American composer who, together with Paul J. Smith, scored many Disney films, such as \"The Apple Dumpling Gang\" in 1975, \"The Apple Dumpling Gang Rides Again\" in 1979, \"The Shaggy D.A.\" in 1976, \"The Many Adventures of Winnie the Pooh\" in 1977, and \"The Fox and the Hound\" in 1981.\nPage: Bruce M. Fischer. Sentence: Fischer also played a rapist in Clint Eastwood's \"The Outlaw Josey Wales\" (1976), and Mr. Coogar in the film \"Something Wicked This Way Comes\" (1983).",
